# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights -- published artifacts, fetched from source, never vendored.
# See Rineya_state_experiment_bundle/README_BUNDLE.md ("Not included").
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Qwen3-0.6B/
qwen3-0.6b/
model/
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.bin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable dataset payloads.
#
# These directories are rebuilt deterministically by the generator shipped
# alongside them and verified against the committed checksum manifests:
#
#   rineya_sequence_independence_dataset_v1  scripts/generate_dataset.py --seed 20260818
#                                            -> data/manifests/sha256sums.txt
#   ..._Corpus_v2.0                          scripts/generate_dataset.py (seed 20260816)
#                                            -> manifests/checksums.sha256
#   ..._Corpus_v3.0                          scripts/generate_dataset.py
#                                            -> manifests/checksums.sha256
#
# Scripts, schemas, manifests, reports, cards and samples ARE tracked, so the
# payload is reproducible from this repository alone. Corpora that ship no
# generator (Rineya_Short_Response_Behavior_Corpus_v1.0, Aegis_RAG_v3_train_4410)
# are committed in full and must not be added here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rineya_state_experiment_bundle/rineya_sequence_independence_dataset_v1/data/full_context/
Rineya_state_experiment_bundle/rineya_sequence_independence_dataset_v1/data/split_transitions/
Rineya_General_Reasoning_and_Natural_Communication_Corpus_v2.0/data/
Rineya_General_Reasoning_and_Natural_Communication_Corpus_v3.0/data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment outputs. Every run is reproducible from a config + seed; the
# artifacts themselves (adapters, eval records, comparison reports) are not
# inputs and must not be versioned.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/
outputs/
data/extracted/
data/derived_views/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build, cache, environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
.venv-crcc-v1/
venv/
.env
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local tooling state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compression + healing derived data. All of it is reproducible from a script,
# a seed and a manifest, so it is not an input and must not be versioned. The
# manifests themselves (mix_manifest.json, trim_manifest.json) ARE tracked --
# they carry the sha256 needed to verify that a rebuild matched.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/heal_mixes/**/*.jsonl
artifacts/heal_runs/**/cache/
artifacts/heal_runs/**/checkpoints/
artifacts/verify_resume/
artifacts/verify_interrupt/

# Imported evaluation payloads. Upstream-owned data, re-importable via
# scripts/eval/import_eval_assets.py; manifests/eval_assets.json carries the
# sha256 for each, including the sealed test set.
artifacts/eval_sets/*.jsonl

# Exported adapters. Re-derivable from a run checkpoint via
# scripts/train/export_adapter.py; export_manifest.json carries the provenance.
artifacts/adapters/**/*.safetensors

# Experiment per-case outputs: bulky (93 MB across 30 runs) and regenerable from
# the scripts. Summaries, per-category breakdowns and manifests ARE tracked.
experiments/**/results/**/results.jsonl
experiments/**/results/*.log

# Copied published cores (2.3 GB each) -- provenance is in artifacts/halo_configs/,
# which is committed. The rule used to name model.safetensors only, which left the
# tokenizer and config files stageable: a single `git add -A` would have vendored a
# second copy of metadata this repo already tracks. Ignore the directories whole.
artifacts/Rineya-Halo-*/
_sel_*__rag_dev/
_modelsmoke*
_adapt*

# queue logs and the single-instance lock: operational, never evidence
experiments/*/results/_logs/